From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:40:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fence TileLang consumer reads before releasing shared stages

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Local-base: b26f48b85790b832993f2c9d240dc3c39d6075e8, the five-patch refresh from deployment PR #875.
Upstream-source: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3537
Upstream-head: d044264967190554349ad5ddebf478f4432478f6

Rationale: Generic-proxy stage reads must finish before a consumer releases the stage for the next async-proxy TMA write. Emit the required proxy fence before consumer release.

Quality: Changes synchronization only. Restrict the fence to generic-proxy reads; preserve the upstream treatment of async-only consumers. No numerical failure or serving speedup is claimed from the sampled workload.

Tests: Two generated-code fence assertions and one SM121 numerical reproducer pass twice.
Recorded compiler tree: 93d54ec9d049abe77cb7d0de3b9ebc1f98ca9951.
See this candidate's results.json and immutable raw receipts. Full image,
retained-feature and serving qualification remain separate gates.

Upstream-status: open PR, checked 2026-11-04; pinned experimental backport.
Remove this local backport when advancing to an upstream revision containing it.
